# Terachess-Stockfish

Terachess-Stockfish is a derivative of Stockfish, adapted to Terachess II
(16x16 board, 26 piece types) by Jean-Louis Cazaux.

## Terachess-Stockfish

David J. (Belzedar94)
  - 256-square board representation, move generation for the 26 Terachess
    piece types, NNUE feature set and network format, embedded data
    generation, training pipeline, verification harness.

## Rules of Terachess

Jean-Louis Cazaux
  - Inventor of Terachess (2008) and Terachess II (2020).
    http://history.chess.free.fr/terachess.htm
  - The rules implemented here follow his specification; the engine and this
    project are not affiliated with or endorsed by him.

H. G. Muller
  - The Interactive Diagram on the chessvariants.com page for Terachess II,
    whose Betza notation was used as the primary machine-readable source when
    writing the rules specification.

## Upstream: Stockfish

Terachess-Stockfish is built on Stockfish, which is Copyright (C) 2004-2026
The Stockfish developers. The full list of Stockfish authors is available at

    https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/blob/master/AUTHORS

Stockfish was originally developed by Tord Romstad, Marco Costalba, Joona
Kiiski and Gary Linscott, and is maintained by the Stockfish community.

The 256-bit bitboard operators were adapted from the very-large-boards branch
of Fairy-Stockfish (Fabian Fichter and contributors, GPLv3), itself a
derivative of Stockfish.

